// A `given` naming a real, resolvable, 0-parameter void setup, with
// casegiven[i] non-empty: fit_given (../../../../given/valid.id) needs one
// case where a case's `given` really did run. "fx_setup" is registered here
// (fn_fixture only registers "fx_target", which takes a parameter and
// returns int, so given_shape would reject it) the way fn_fixture_reg
// registers "fx_target" itself. Paired with impcase_empty (../../../fit/
// fit.id, room for only one of the two there).
impcase_given() {
  fn_fixture();
  int[] none = [];
  int setup_node = node_func("fx_setup", "void", none, none, 0 - 1);
} chain () {
  push((import fnames), "fx_setup");
  push((import fnodes), setup_node);
  push((import casegiven), "fx_setup");
} return void;
